<title>BRAZIL: August sees record Brazil petroleum use - Petrobras.</title>
<headline>August sees record Brazil petroleum use - Petrobras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumption in Brazil of petroleum products averaged a record 1,577,500 barrels per day (bpd) in August, up 0.3 percent from July, state-controlled energy monopoly Petrobras said in a statement.</p>
<p>The figure also represents a 1.2 percent increase on the same month last year, it added.</p>
<p>Of the total, diesel accounted for 546,200 barrels bpd and gasoline 266,500 bpd, it said.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
